{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba probe_rehearsal.py; cat rehearsal.log'","aggregated_output":"     1\t\"\"\"The paid acceptance probe's $0 rehearsal (PROBE-DESIGN.md v5 §4; D716): `probe.Probe` runs unchanged on the real budget transport\n     2\tand ledger, with `model.openai_transport` replaced by a stub that checks every request's bytes and counts the calls.\n     3\t\n     4\t  python3 probe.py rehearse <new out folder> <scenario>\n     5\t  scenarios: clean, format-invalid, a1-400, a1-timeout, 5xx-then-ok, low-ceiling, retry-exhausts, mutant-open-b, checks, verdicts, all\n     6\t\"\"\"\n     7\timport json\n     8\timport os\n     9\timport sys\n    10\timport tempfile\n    11\tfrom pathlib import Path\n    12\t\n    13\tHERE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\n    14\tREPO = HERE.parents[2]\n    15\tsys.path.insert(0, str(HERE))\n    16\tsys.path.insert(0, str(REPO / 'tests'))\n    17\timport probe                                                            # noqa: E402\n    18\timport probe_read                                                       # noqa: E402\n    19\tfrom hivemind import model                                              # noqa: E402\n    20\tfrom hivemind.views import judging                                     # noqa: E402\n    21\t\n    22\tPLAN = json.loads(probe.PLAN.read_text())\n    23\tITEMS = {i['user']: i for i in PLAN['acceptance'] + PLAN['refused'] + PLAN['matched']}\n    24\t\n    25\t\n    26\tdef valid_answer(item, form, drop_marker=None):\n    27\t    lists = item['lists']\n    28\t    previous = __import__('re').search(r'^\\[Previous conclusion, for comparison only\\] rung (\\d+);', item['user'], __import__('re').M)\n    29\t    cites = lists['evidence'][:3]\n    30\t    reasons = 'scripted reasons; the consensus growth estimate of 85.4% sits at rung 1; $393 billion is the reference.'\n    31\t    if drop_marker:\n    32\t        reasons = reasons.replace(drop_marker, 'an earlier figure')\n    33\t    return {'rung': int(previous.group(1)) if previous else 1, 'reference': 'scripted reference', 'implied_outcome': 'scripted outcome',\n    34\t            'reasons': reasons, 'cites': cites, 'cites_views': [], 'pushes': [{'evidence_id': e, 'push': 'none'} for e in cites],\n    35\t            'changed': previous is None, 'why_changed': 'scripted', 'theme_pushes': [{'view_id': t, 'push': 'none'} for t in lists['themes'][:1]]}\n    36\t\n    37\t\n    38\tclass Stub:\n    39\t    \"\"\"Checks each request (system and user as stored, the format strict and exactly the planned one, the setting as poc-v121's),\n    40\t    counts calls per (request, format) and answers by scenario.\"\"\"\n    41\t\n    42\t    def __init__(self, cfg, scenario):\n    43\t        self.cfg, self.scenario, self.calls, self.problems, self.seen = cfg, scenario, {}, [], set()\n    44\t\n    45\t    def __call__(self, provider, request, max_attempts=1, timeout=180):\n    46\t        user = request['messages'][1]['content']\n    47\t        item = ITEMS.get(user)\n    48\t        if item is None or request['messages'][0]['content'] != item['system']:\n    49\t            self.problems.append('a request whose text is not a planned one')\n    50\t            raise model.TransportError('unplanned request')\n    51\t        schema = request['response_format']['json_schema']['schema']\n    52\t        expected_v12, expected_v7 = judging.schema_for('judging-v12', item['lists']), judging.schema_for('judging-v7')   # never the code under test\n    53\t        form = 'v12' if schema == expected_v12 else ('v7' if schema == expected_v7 else None)\n    54\t        key = probe.key_of(item)\n    55\t        part = 'B' if item in PLAN['refused'] else ('C' if item in PLAN['matched'] else 'A')\n    56\t        if form is None or (part in ('A', 'B') and form != 'v12'):\n    57\t            self.problems.append(f'{key}: the format is not the planned one for part {part}')\n    58\t        if request['response_format'].get('type') != 'json_schema' or request['response_format']['json_schema'].get('strict') is not True \\\n    59\t                or request['response_format']['json_schema'].get('name') != 'judgement':\n    60\t            self.problems.append(f'{key}: the format is not strict json_schema named judgement')\n    61\t        if (request['model'], request.get('reasoning_effort'), request.get('max_completion_tokens')) != \\\n    62\t                (self.cfg.rejudging.model, self.cfg.rejudging.reasoning_effort, self.cfg.rejudging.max_output_tokens):\n    63\t            self.problems.append(f'{key}: the model settings differ from poc-v121')\n    64\t        count_key = (key, form)\n    65\t        self.calls[count_key] = self.calls.get(count_key, 0) + 1\n    66\t        attempt = self.calls[count_key]\n    67\t        s = self.scenario\n    68\t        if s == 'a1-400' and key == 'old-1:5652':\n    69\t            error = model.TransportError('HTTP 400: invalid schema'); error.http_status = 400\n    70\t            raise error\n    71\t        if s == 'a1-timeout' and key == 'old-1:5652':\n    72\t            raise model.TransportError('timed out')\n    73\t        if s == '5xx-then-ok' and key == 'old-3:69' and attempt == 1:\n    74\t            error = model.TransportError('HTTP 503'); error.http_status = 503\n    75\t            raise error\n    76\t        if s == 'retry-exhausts' and part == 'C' and key == PLAN['matched'][0]['source'] + ':' + str(PLAN['matched'][0]['call_id']) and form == 'v12' and attempt == 2:\n    77\t            error = model.TransportError('HTTP 503'); error.http_status = 503\n    78\t            raise error\n    79\t        data = valid_answer(item, form, drop_marker='85.4' if s == 'clean' and key == 'control-1:8938' and attempt == 1 else None)\n    80\t        if s == 'format-invalid' and key == 'old-2:591' and attempt == 1:\n    81\t            data['cites'] = data['cites'] + ['e999999']\n    82\t        usage = {'prompt_tokens': 1000, 'completion_tokens': 100}\n    83\t        if s == 'retry-exhausts' and part == 'C':                      # each answer costs its full reservation, so a retry's extra charge exhausts the headroom\n    84\t            usage = {'prompt_tokens': 2 * len(json.dumps(request).encode('utf-8')) + 4096, 'completion_tokens': request['max_completion_tokens']}\n    85\t        return {'choices': [{'message': {'content': json.dumps(data)}}], 'usage': usage}\n    86\t\n    87\t\n    88\tdef run(out, scenario):\n    89\t    budget = probe.budget_module()\n    90\t    out.mkdir(parents=True)\n    91\t    ledger_path = out / 'ledger.json'\n    92\t    budget.SharedLedger.init(str(ledger_path), probe.APPROVED_CEILING)\n    93\t    ledger = budget.SharedLedger(str(ledger_path))\n    94\t    p = probe.Probe(out, budget.BudgetTransport(ledger, sleep=lambda seconds: None), ledger, budget)\n    95\t    stub = Stub(p.cfg, scenario)\n    96\t    original_transport, original_format = model.openai_transport, probe.answer_format\n    97\t    model.openai_transport = stub\n    98\t    if scenario == 'mutant-open-b':\n    99\t        probe.answer_format = lambda item, form: judging.schema_for('judging-v7') if item in PLAN['refused'] else original_format(item, form)\n   100\t    first_c = probe.schedule(PLAN)[3][1][0]\n   101\t    need_c1 = sum(p.reservation(s) for s in first_c)\n   102\t    original_run_group = p.headroom\n   103\t\n   104\t    def lowered():\n   105\t        state = ledger.read()\n   106\t        if scenario in ('low-ceiling', 'retry-exhausts') and not getattr(lowered, 'done', False) and \\\n   107\t                sum(1 for line in (out / 'answers.jsonl').read_text().splitlines() if '\"part\": \"B\"' in line) == 48:\n   108\t            ceiling = state['spent'] + (need_c1 * 0.5 if scenario == 'low-ceiling' else need_c1 + 0.0005)\n   109\t            with ledger._locked() as s:\n   110\t                s['ceiling'] = ceiling\n   111\t            lowered.done = True\n   112\t        return original_run_group()\n   113\t    p.headroom = lowered\n   114\t    try:\n   115\t        summary = p.run(PLAN)\n   116\t    finally:\n   117\t        model.openai_transport, probe.answer_format = original_transport, original_format\n   118\t    answers = probe_read.load_answers(out)\n   119\t    return summary, stub, answers\n   120\t\n   121\t\n   122\tdef expect(name, condition, detail=''):\n   123\t    print(f'  [{\"ok\" if condition else \"FAIL\"}] {name}{(\": \" + detail) if detail and not condition else \"\"}')\n   124\t    return bool(condition)\n   125\t\n   126\t\n   127\tdef scenario_checks(out, scenario):\n   128\t    summary, stub, answers = run(out / scenario, scenario)\n   129\t    statuses = [a['status'] for a in answers.values()]\n   130\t    ok = True\n   131\t    print(scenario)\n   132\t    if scenario == 'clean':\n   133\t        ok &= expect('no request problem', not stub.problems, str(stub.problems[:3]))\n   134\t        ok &= expect('2 + 48 + 72 + A2 answers', sum(1 for a in answers.values() if a['part'] in ('A1', 'A0')) == 2 and\n   135\t                     sum(1 for a in answers.values() if a['part'] == 'B') == 48 and sum(1 for a in answers.values() if a['part'] == 'C') == 72 and summary['A2'] == 'answered')\n   136\t        ok &= expect('three fresh stub calls per planned request and format', all(v == 3 for (k, f), v in stub.calls.items()\n   137\t                     if not k.startswith(('old-1:5652', 'old-3:69', 'sealed')) and f is not None), str({k: v for k, v in stub.calls.items() if v != 3}))\n   138\t        ok &= expect('every answer answered and passing the request-time check', all(a['status'] == 'answered' and not a['check'] and not a['cached'] for a in answers.values()))\n   139\t        probe_read.packets(out / scenario)\n   140\t        packet = json.loads((out / scenario / 'packet-B.json').read_text())\n   141\t        flagged = [e for e in packet if e['id'].startswith('control-1:8938|') and e['id'].endswith('|e362') and '85.4' in e['markers not found']]\n   142\t        ok &= expect('the 8938 packet flags the one answer that drops 85.4', len(flagged) == 1)\n   143\t    elif scenario == 'format-invalid':\n   144\t        ok &= expect('the format-invalid answer takes the SchemaError path', answers[('B', 'old-2:591', 'v12', 1)]['status'] == 'format invalid')\n   145\t    elif scenario == 'a1-400':\n   146\t        ok &= expect('A1 recorded as a 400', answers[('A1', 'old-1:5652', 'v12', 1)].get('http_status') == 400)\n   147\t    elif scenario == 'a1-timeout':\n   148\t        line = answers[('A1', 'old-1:5652', 'v12', 1)]\n   149\t        ok &= expect('A1 recorded as a transport error without a status, after three attempts', line['status'] == 'transport error' and line.get('http_status') is None\n   150\t                     and stub.calls[('old-1:5652', 'v12')] == 3)\n   151\t    elif scenario == '5xx-then-ok':\n   152\t        ok &= expect('A0 answered after a 503 retry', answers[('A0', 'old-3:69', 'v12', 1)]['status'] == 'answered' and stub.calls[('old-3:69', 'v12')] == 2)\n   153\t    elif scenario == 'low-ceiling':\n   154\t        ok &= expect('the first Part C comparison is not started', summary['not started'] and summary['not started'][0]['key'] == probe.key_of(PLAN['matched'][0]))\n   155\t    elif scenario == 'retry-exhausts':\n   156\t        ok &= expect('the admitted comparison is interrupted by the refused retry reservation', summary['interrupted'] == [probe.key_of(PLAN['matched'][0])]\n   157\t                     and summary['ledger']['stopped'])\n   158\t    elif scenario == 'mutant-open-b':\n   159\t        ok &= expect('the byte check catches Part B sent with the open format', any('not the planned one for part B' in p for p in stub.problems))\n   160\t    if scenario in ('low-ceiling', 'retry-exhausts', 'a1-timeout', 'a1-400'):\n   161\t        readings = clean_readings()\n   162\t        result = probe_read.verdict(answers, readings, PLAN, json.loads(probe_read.TARGETS.read_text()), json.loads(probe_read.STORED_V7.read_text()), summary)\n   163\t        expected = 'not ready (format)' if scenario == 'a1-400' else 'inconclusive (incomplete)'\n   164\t        ok &= expect(f'verdict {expected}', result[0] == expected, str(result))\n   165\t    return ok\n   166\t\n   167\t\n   168\tdef clean_readings(overrides=None):\n   169\t    targets = json.loads(probe_read.TARGETS.read_text())\n   170\t    b = {}\n   171\t    for request in targets['requests']:\n   172\t        for d in (1, 2, 3):\n   173\t            for target in request['targets']:\n   174\t                cls = 'ambiguous' if target.get('ambiguous') else ('intended' if target['kind'] == 'evidence' else 'correct')\n   175\t                b[f'{request[\"key\"]}|{d}|{probe_read.target_ids(target)}'] = {'class': cls, 'valid_support': target['kind'] == 'evidence'}\n   176\t    c = {probe.key_of(i): {'read': True, 'harms': []} for i in PLAN['matched']}\n   177\t    readings = {'B': b, 'C': c}\n   178\t    for key, value in (overrides or {}).items():\n   179\t        part, name = key.split('/', 1)\n   180\t        if value is None:\n   181\t            readings[part].pop(name, None)\n   182\t        else:\n   183\t            readings[part][name] = value\n   184\t    return readings\n   185\t\n   186\t\n   187\tdef clean_answers():\n   188\t    answers = {}\n   189\t    for part, specs in probe.schedule(PLAN):\n   190\t        flat = [s for group in specs for s in (group if isinstance(group, list) else [group])]\n   191\t        for s in flat:\n   192\t            answers[(s['part'], s['key'], s['form'], s['draw'])] = {'part': s['part'], 'key': s['key'], 'form': s['form'], 'draw': s['draw'],\n   193\t                                                                     'status': 'answered', 'check': []}\n   194\t    return answers\n   195\t\n   196\t\n   197\tdef verdict_cases():\n   198\t    targets, stored = json.loads(probe_read.TARGETS.read_text()), json.loads(probe_read.STORED_V7.read_text())\n   199\t    clean_summary = {'ledger': {'stopped': False}}\n   200\t    v = lambda answers, readings, summary=clean_summary: probe_read.verdict(answers, readings, PLAN, targets, stored, summary)[0]\n   201\t    unsupported = lambda key, bad: {f'B/{key}|{d}|{bad}': {'class': 'unsupported', 'valid_support': False} for d in (1, 2, 3)}\n   202\t    misattributed = {f'B/old-2:591|{d}|e88': {'class': 'misattributed', 'valid_support': True} for d in (1, 2, 3)}\n   203\t    two_wrong_one_omitted = {'B/control-1:8807|1|e393': {'class': 'misattributed', 'valid_support': False},\n   204\t                             'B/control-1:8807|2|e393': {'class': 'misattributed', 'valid_support': False},\n   205\t                             'B/control-1:8807|3|e393': {'class': 'omitted', 'valid_support': False}}\n   206\t    missing_two = dict(clean_answers())\n   207\t    for d in (2, 3):\n   208\t        missing_two.pop(('B', 'control-1:8807', 'v12', d))\n   209\t    a1_400 = dict(clean_answers()); a1_400[('A1', 'old-1:5652', 'v12', 1)] = dict(a1_400[('A1', 'old-1:5652', 'v12', 1)], status='transport error', http_status=400, error='HTTP 400')\n   210\t    a1_timeout = dict(clean_answers()); a1_timeout[('A1', 'old-1:5652', 'v12', 1)] = dict(a1_timeout[('A1', 'old-1:5652', 'v12', 1)], status='transport error', http_status=None)\n   211\t    c_incomplete = dict(clean_answers()); c_incomplete.pop(('C', probe.key_of(PLAN['matched'][-1]), 'v7', 3))\n   212\t    a2_skipped = dict(clean_answers()); a2_skipped.pop(('A2', 'sealed-D358:6918', 'v12', 1), None)\n   213\t    a2_rejected = dict(clean_answers()); a2_rejected[('A2', 'sealed-D358:6918', 'v12', 1)] = {'part': 'A2', 'key': 'sealed-D358:6918', 'form': 'v12', 'draw': 1, 'status': 'transport error', 'http_status': 400}\n   214\t    refused_one = dict(clean_answers())\n   215\t    refused_one[('B', 'old-2:591', 'v12', 1)] = {'part': 'B', 'key': 'old-2:591', 'form': 'v12', 'draw': 1, 'status': 'answered', 'check': ['x']}\n   216\t    cases = [\n   217\t        ('clean set', v(clean_answers(), clean_readings()), 'pass'),\n   218\t        ('8938 85.4% unsupported in three draws', v(clean_answers(), clean_readings(unsupported('control-1:8938', 'e362'))), 'inconclusive (unresolved)'),\n   219\t        ('8807 $393B unsupported in three draws', v(clean_answers(), clean_readings(unsupported('control-1:8807', 'e393'))), 'not ready'),\n   220\t        ('three misattributions', v(clean_answers(), clean_readings(misattributed)), 'not ready'),\n   221\t        ('8807 two wrong, one omitted', v(clean_answers(), clean_readings(two_wrong_one_omitted)), 'not ready'),\n   222\t        ('8807 one unsupported, two missing', v(missing_two, clean_readings({'B/control-1:8807|1|e393': {'class': 'unsupported', 'valid_support': False},\n   223\t                                                                             'B/control-1:8807|2|e393': None, 'B/control-1:8807|3|e393': None})), 'inconclusive (incomplete)'),\n   224\t        ('A1 rejected', v(a1_400, clean_readings()), 'not ready (format)'),\n   225\t        ('A1 timed out', v(a1_timeout, clean_readings()), 'inconclusive (incomplete)'),\n   226\t        ('misattribution excess with Part C incomplete', v(c_incomplete, clean_readings(misattributed)), 'not ready'),\n   227\t        ('unresolved Part C difference, all else clean', v(clean_answers(), clean_readings({f'C/{probe.key_of(PLAN[\"matched\"][0])}': {'read': True, 'harms': [{'kind': 'a', 'status': 'unresolved'}]}})), 'inconclusive (unresolved)'),\n   228\t        ('A2 skipped', v(a2_skipped, clean_readings()), 'pass'),\n   229\t        ('A2 rejected', v(a2_rejected, clean_readings()), 'pass'),\n   230\t        ('a refused v12 answer', v(refused_one, clean_readings()), 'not ready'),\n   231\t        ('a ledger stop', v(clean_answers(), clean_readings(), {'ledger': {'stopped': True, 'stop_reason': 'ceiling'}}), 'inconclusive (incomplete)'),\n   232\t    ]\n   233\t    ok = True\n   234\t    print('verdicts')\n   235\t    for name, got, want in cases:\n   236\t        ok &= expect(f'{name} -> {want}', got == want, got)\n   237\t    return ok\n   238\t\n   239\t\n   240\tdef check_equivalence():\n   241\t    \"\"\"check_at_request equals judging.check_answer on a ledger whose state is known, and on the planned requests' stored answers.\"\"\"\n   242\t    import test_theme_block as fixtures\n   243\t    ok = True\n   244\t    print('checks')\n   245\t    with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as scratch:\n   246\t        conn = fixtures.ledger(Path(scratch))\n   247\t        fixtures.judged(conn, 'v2', 1, 'theme judged', 2)\n   248\t        conn.commit()\n   249\t        _, user, lists = judging.request_parts(conn, 'v1', 'judging-v12')\n   250\t        base = {'rung': 2, 'reference': 'r', 'implied_outcome': 'o', 'reasons': 'x', 'cites': ['e1'], 'cites_views': [], 'pushes': [], 'changed': True,\n   251\t                'why_changed': 'w', 'theme_pushes': [{'view_id': 'v2', 'push': 'none'}]}\n   252\t        variants = [base, dict(base, rung=9), dict(base, changed=False), dict(base, reference=''), dict(base, cites=['e9']),\n   253\t                    dict(base, theme_pushes=[{'view_id': 'v2', 'push': 'none'}] * 2), dict(base, cites_views=['v3'])]\n   254\t        for data in variants:\n   255\t            ok &= expect(f'equal on {json.dumps({k: data[k] for k in data if data[k] != base.get(k)})}',\n   256\t                         probe.check_at_request(data, user, lists) == judging.check_answer(conn, 'v1', data, user, lists))\n   257\t        fixtures.judged(conn, 'v1', 3, 'first', 3)\n   258\t        conn.commit()\n   259\t        _, user, lists = judging.request_parts(conn, 'v1', 'judging-v12')\n   260\t        for data in (dict(base, rung=2, changed=False), dict(base, rung=3, changed=False)):\n   261\t            ok &= expect(f'equal with a previous conclusion, rung {data[\"rung\"]} changed false',\n   262\t                         probe.check_at_request(data, user, lists) == judging.check_answer(conn, 'v1', data, user, lists))\n   263\t    stored_ok = all(not probe.check_at_request(json.loads(i['stored answer']), i['user'], i['lists']) for i in PLAN['matched'])\n   264\t    ok &= expect('every planned matched request\\'s stored committed answer passes (linked-1 8834 included)', stored_ok)\n   265\t    bad = [i for i in PLAN['refused'] if not all(any(b in e for e in probe.check_at_request(json.loads(i['stored answer']), i['user'], i['lists'])) for b in i['bad ids'] if b in json.dumps(json.loads(i['stored answer'])))]\n   266\t    ok &= expect('every planned refused request\\'s stored answer is refused on its bad ids', not bad, str([probe.key_of(i) for i in bad]))\n   267\t    return ok\n   268\t\n   269\t\n   270\tdef main(out, scenario):\n   271\t    if out.exists():\n   272\t        raise SystemExit(f'{out} exists: a rehearsal starts from an empty folder')\n   273\t    out.mkdir(parents=True)\n   274\t    names = ['clean', 'format-invalid', 'a1-400', 'a1-timeout', '5xx-then-ok', 'low-ceiling', 'retry-exhausts', 'mutant-open-b'] if scenario == 'all' else [scenario]\n   275\t    ok = True\n   276\t    if scenario in ('all', 'checks'):\n   277\t        ok &= check_equivalence()\n   278\t    if scenario in ('all', 'verdicts'):\n   279\t        ok &= verdict_cases()\n   280\t    for name in names:\n   281\t        if name in ('checks', 'verdicts'):\n   282\t            continue\n   283\t        ok &= scenario_checks(out, name)\n   284\t    print('REHEARSAL', 'PASS' if ok else 'FAIL')\n   285\t    sys.exit(0 if ok else 1)\nchecks\n  [ok] equal on {}\n  [ok] equal on {\"rung\": 9}\n  [ok] equal on {\"changed\": false}\n  [ok] equal on {\"reference\": \"\"}\n  [ok] equal on {\"cites\": [\"e9\"]}\n  [ok] equal on {\"theme_pushes\": [{\"view_id\": \"v2\", \"push\": \"none\"}, {\"view_id\": \"v2\", \"push\": \"none\"}]}\n  [ok] equal on {\"cites_views\": [\"v3\"]}\n  [ok] equal with a previous conclusion, rung 2 changed false\n  [ok] equal with a previous conclusion, rung 3 changed false\n  [ok] every planned matched request's stored committed answer passes (linked-1 8834 included)\n  [ok] every planned refused request's stored answer is refused on its bad ids\nverdicts\n  [ok] clean set -> pass\n  [ok] 8938 85.4% unsupported in three draws -> inconclusive (unresolved)\n  [ok] 8807 $393B unsupported in three draws -> not ready\n  [ok] three misattributions -> not ready\n  [ok] 8807 two wrong, one omitted -> not ready\n  [ok] 8807 one unsupported, two missing -> inconclusive (incomplete)\n  [ok] A1 rejected -> not ready (format)\n  [ok] A1 timed out -> inconclusive (incomplete)\n  [ok] misattribution excess with Part C incomplete -> not ready\n  [ok] unresolved Part C difference, all else clean -> inconclusive (unresolved)\n  [ok] A2 skipped -> pass\n  [ok] A2 rejected -> pass\n  [ok] a refused v12 answer -> not ready\n  [ok] a ledger stop -> inconclusive (incomplete)\nclean\n  [ok] no request problem\n  [ok] 2 + 48 + 72 + A2 answers\n  [ok] three fresh stub calls per planned request and format\n  [ok] every answer answered and passing the request-time check\nPart B: 51 target readings; Part C: 12 comparisons\n  [ok] the 8938 packet flags the one answer that drops 85.4\nformat-invalid\n  [ok] the format-invalid answer takes the SchemaError path\na1-400\n  [ok] A1 recorded as a 400\n  [ok] verdict not ready (format)\na1-timeout\n  [ok] A1 recorded as a transport error without a status, after three attempts\n  [ok] verdict inconclusive (incomplete)\n5xx-then-ok\n  [ok] A0 answered after a 503 retry\nlow-ceiling\n  [ok] the first Part C comparison is not started\n  [ok] verdict inconclusive (incomplete)\nretry-exhausts\n  [ok] the admitted comparison is interrupted by the refused retry reservation\n  [ok] verdict inconclusive (incomplete)\nmutant-open-b\n  [ok] the byte check catches Part B sent with the open format\nREHEARSAL PASS\nexit 0\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba probe.py; nl -ba probe_read.py'","aggregated_output":"     1\t\"\"\"The paid acceptance probe of judging-v12 (PROBE-DESIGN.md v5, D715, D716). Harness-only; nothing here is product code.\n     2\t\n     3\t  python3 probe.py send <new out folder> <approved ceiling>     # paid: refuses any ceiling but Alex's $0.50\n     4\t  python3 probe.py rehearse <new out folder> <scenario>         # $0: the provider stubbed beneath the real budget transport\n     5\t\n     6\tOrder (§2): A1, A0; Part B (16 refused requests x 3 under v12, 4 at a time); Part C (12 comparisons, cheapest first, one at a time,\n     7\teach starting only when the ledger's headroom covers its six first attempts' reservations; its six sends one after another); A2 last\n     8\tand only when the headroom covers its reservation. Every send has its own archive, so no draw is answered from an earlier one. Each\n     9\tanswer goes through `model.call` (the format check) and the request-time check, and is written to answers.jsonl.\n    10\t\"\"\"\n    11\timport concurrent.futures\n    12\timport importlib.util\n    13\timport json\n    14\timport re\n    15\timport sys\n    16\timport threading\n    17\tfrom pathlib import Path\n    18\t\n    19\tHERE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\n    20\tREPO = HERE.parents[2]\n    21\tsys.path.insert(0, str(REPO / 'src'))\n    22\tfrom hivemind import config, model                                      # noqa: E402\n    23\tfrom hivemind.views import judging                                     # noqa: E402\n    24\t\n    25\tPLAN = HERE / 'probe-plan.json'\n    26\tV121 = REPO / 'poc/config/poc-v121.json'\n    27\tAPPROVED_CEILING = 0.50                                                 # Alex, D715\n    28\tB_WORKERS = 4\n    29\tEXPECTED = {'A': 2, 'B': 48, 'C': 72}\n    30\t\n    31\t\n    32\tdef budget_module():\n    33\t    spec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location('budget_replay_probe', REPO / 'clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py')\n    34\t    module = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)\n    35\t    spec.loader.exec_module(module)\n    36\t    return module\n    37\t\n    38\t\n    39\tdef key_of(item):\n    40\t    return f'{item[\"source\"]}:{item[\"call_id\"]}'\n    41\t\n    42\t\n    43\tdef answer_format(item, form):\n    44\t    return judging.schema_for('judging-v12', item['lists']) if form == 'v12' else judging.schema_for('judging-v7')\n    45\t\n    46\t\n    47\tdef header_counts(user):\n    48\t    \"\"\"(evidence entries the header announces, themes the header announces): the text-read lists must match them.\"\"\"\n    49\t    evidence = re.search(r'\\[Evidence in view under this thesis, (\\d+) items\\]', user)\n    50\t    themes = re.search(r'\\[Themes in force, (\\d+)\\]', user)\n    51\t    return (int(evidence.group(1)) if evidence else None), (int(themes.group(1)) if themes else 0)\n    52\t\n    53\t\n    54\tdef check_at_request(data, user, lists):\n    55\t    \"\"\"`judging.check_answer` as at request time: membership against the request's lists; the rung range from its ladder line;\n    56\t    first-judgement and changed from its previous-conclusion line; the stance fields; duplicate theme pushes. Same messages.\"\"\"\n    57\t    view_id = re.match(r'Thesis (v\\d+) \\(', user).group(1)\n    58\t    errors, named = [], []\n    59\t    for entry in data.get('theme_pushes', []):\n    60\t        if entry['view_id'] in named:\n    61\t            errors.append(f'{entry[\"view_id\"]} is named twice in theme_pushes')\n    62\t        elif entry['view_id'] not in lists['themes']:\n    63\t            errors.append(f'{entry[\"view_id\"]} is not a theme in force shown to {view_id}')\n    64\t        named.append(entry['view_id'])\n    65\t    ladder = re.search(r'^Ladder: (.*)$', user, re.M).group(1)\n    66\t    rung_count = len(re.findall(r'(?:^|/ )rung \\d+ ', ladder))\n    67\t    if not 1 <= data['rung'] <= rung_count:\n    68\t        errors.append(f'rung {data[\"rung\"]} outside 1..{rung_count}')\n    69\t    for cited in data['cites']:\n    70\t        if cited not in lists['evidence']:\n    71\t            errors.append(f'{cited} is not among the evidence shown to {view_id}')\n    72\t    for cited in data['cites_views']:\n    73\t        if cited not in lists['dependencies']:\n    74\t            errors.append(f'{cited} is not a dependency of {view_id}')\n    75\t    for push in data['pushes']:\n    76\t        if push['evidence_id'] not in lists['evidence']:\n    77\t            errors.append(f'push on {push[\"evidence_id\"]} which was not shown to {view_id}')\n    78\t    for field in judging.STANCE_FIELDS:\n    79\t        if not str(data.get(field) or '').strip():\n    80\t            errors.append(f'{field} is empty: state what the market expects and the figure or date the evidence implies')\n    81\t    previous = re.search(r'^\\[Previous conclusion, for comparison only\\] rung (\\d+);', user, re.M)\n    82\t    if previous is None and '\\n[Previous conclusion] none: this is the first judgement' in user and not data['changed']:\n    83\t        errors.append('first judgement must say changed')\n    84\t    if previous is not None and int(previous.group(1)) != data['rung'] and not data['changed']:\n    85\t        errors.append(f'rung moved from {previous.group(1)} to {data[\"rung\"]} but changed is false')\n    86\t    return errors\n    87\t\n    88\t\n    89\tdef schedule(plan):\n    90\t    \"\"\"The sends in order, grouped: [('A1', [spec]), ('A0', ...), ('B', [48 specs]), ('C', [[6 specs] x 12]), ('A2', [spec])].\"\"\"\n    91\t    spec = lambda part, item, form, draw: {'part': part, 'key': key_of(item), 'form': form, 'draw': draw, 'item': item}\n    92\t    a1, a0, a2 = plan['acceptance']\n    93\t    b = [spec('B', item, 'v12', d) for item in plan['refused'] for d in (1, 2, 3)]\n    94\t    c = [[spec('C', item, form, d) for form in ('v12', 'v7') for d in (1, 2, 3)] for item in plan['matched']]\n    95\t    return [('A1', [spec('A1', a1, 'v12', 1)]), ('A0', [spec('A0', a0, 'v12', 1)]), ('B', b), ('C', c), ('A2', [spec('A2', a2, 'v12', 1)])]\n    96\t\n    97\t\n    98\tclass Probe:\n    99\t    def __init__(self, out, transport, ledger, budget):\n   100\t        self.out, self.transport, self.ledger, self.budget = out, transport, ledger, budget\n   101\t        self.cfg = config.load(str(V121))\n   102\t        self.lock = threading.Lock()\n   103\t        (out / 'archives').mkdir(parents=True)\n   104\t\n   105\t    def request(self, spec):\n   106\t        return model.build_request(self.cfg.rejudging, spec['item']['system'], spec['item']['user'], answer_format(spec['item'], spec['form']),\n   107\t                                   'judgement', self.cfg.provider)\n   108\t\n   109\t    def reservation(self, spec):\n   110\t        return self.budget.llm_estimate(self.request(spec))\n   111\t\n   112\t    def headroom(self):\n   113\t        state = self.ledger.read()\n   114\t        return state['ceiling'] - state['spent'] - state['reserved'], state\n   115\t\n   116\t    def record(self, line):\n   117\t        with self.lock, open(self.out / 'answers.jsonl', 'a') as handle:\n   118\t            handle.write(json.dumps(line, ensure_ascii=False) + '\\n')\n   119\t\n   120\t    def send(self, spec):\n   121\t        item, form = spec['item'], spec['form']\n   122\t        name = f'{spec[\"part\"]}-{spec[\"key\"].replace(\":\", \"-\")}-{form}-{spec[\"draw\"]}.sqlite'\n   123\t        archive = model.Archive(str(self.out / 'archives' / name))\n   124\t        line = {k: spec[k] for k in ('part', 'key', 'form', 'draw')}\n   125\t        line['request_sha256'] = model.request_identity(self.request(spec))[1]\n   126\t        try:\n   127\t            answer = model.call(archive, self.cfg, self.cfg.rejudging, item['system'], item['user'], answer_format(item, form), 'judgement', 'judge',\n   128\t                                transport=self.transport)\n   129\t            line.update(status='answered', data=answer.data, cost_usd=answer.cost_usd, cached=answer.cached,\n   130\t                        check=check_at_request(answer.data, item['user'], item['lists']))\n   131\t        except model.SchemaError as error:\n   132\t            row = archive.conn.execute('select answer_json from model_calls order by call_id desc limit 1').fetchone()\n   133\t            line.update(status='format invalid', error=str(error)[:500], data=json.loads(row[0]) if row and row[0] else None)\n   134\t        except model.TransportError as error:\n   135\t            line.update(status='transport error', error=str(error)[:500], http_status=getattr(error, 'http_status', None))\n   136\t        self.record(line)\n   137\t        return line\n   138\t\n   139\t    def run(self, plan):\n   140\t        for item in plan['acceptance'][:2] + plan['refused'] + plan['matched']:\n   141\t            evidence, themes = header_counts(item['user'])\n   142\t            if evidence is not None and (evidence != len(item['lists']['evidence']) or themes != len(item['lists']['themes'])):\n   143\t                raise SystemExit(f'{key_of(item)}: the text-read lists do not match the header counts; not sent')\n   144\t        summary = {'sent': {}, 'not started': [], 'interrupted': [], 'A2': None}\n   145\t        for group, specs in schedule(plan):\n   146\t            if group in ('A1', 'A0'):\n   147\t                summary['sent'][group] = [self.send(s)['status'] for s in specs]\n   148\t            elif group == 'B':\n   149\t                with concurrent.futures.ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=B_WORKERS) as pool:\n   150\t                    summary['sent']['B'] = [line['status'] for line in pool.map(self.send, specs)]\n   151\t            elif group == 'C':\n   152\t                summary['sent']['C'] = []\n   153\t                for comparison in specs:\n   154\t                    need = sum(self.reservation(s) for s in comparison)\n   155\t                    room, state = self.headroom()\n   156\t                    if state.get('stopped') or room < need:\n   157\t                        summary['not started'].append({'key': comparison[0]['key'], 'need': round(need, 4), 'headroom': round(room, 4)})\n   158\t                        continue\n   159\t                    statuses = []\n   160\t                    for s in comparison:\n   161\t                        statuses.append(self.send(s)['status'])\n   162\t                        if statuses[-1] == 'transport error':\n   163\t                            summary['interrupted'].append(comparison[0]['key'])\n   164\t                            break\n   165\t                    summary['sent']['C'].append({'key': comparison[0]['key'], 'statuses': statuses})\n   166\t            else:\n   167\t                need = self.reservation(specs[0])\n   168\t                room, state = self.headroom()\n   169\t                summary['A2'] = self.send(specs[0])['status'] if not state.get('stopped') and room >= need else f'skipped (headroom {room:.4f} < {need:.4f})'\n   170\t        summary['ledger'] = self.ledger.read()\n   171\t        (self.out / 'run-summary.json').write_text(json.dumps(summary, indent=1))\n   172\t        return summary\n   173\t\n   174\t\n   175\tdef send(out, approved):\n   176\t    if approved != APPROVED_CEILING:\n   177\t        raise SystemExit(f'the approved ceiling is ${APPROVED_CEILING} (D715); refused')\n   178\t    if out.exists():\n   179\t        raise SystemExit(f'{out} exists: the probe starts from an empty folder')\n   180\t    out.mkdir(parents=True)\n   181\t    budget = budget_module()\n   182\t    ledger_path = out / 'ledger.json'\n   183\t    budget.SharedLedger.init(str(ledger_path), approved)\n   184\t    ledger = budget.SharedLedger(str(ledger_path))\n   185\t    lock_handle = open(out / 'probe.launcher.lock', 'a+')\n   186\t    if not ledger.claim_launcher('probe', lock_handle):\n   187\t        raise SystemExit('another launch is running')\n   188\t    remove_gate = budget.install_stop_gate(ledger)\n   189\t    try:\n   190\t        summary = Probe(out, budget.BudgetTransport(ledger), ledger, budget).run(json.loads(PLAN.read_text()))\n   191\t    finally:\n   192\t        remove_gate()\n   193\t        ledger.remove_launcher('probe')\n   194\t    print(json.dumps(summary, indent=1)[:4000])\n   195\t\n   196\t\n   197\tif __name__ == '__main__':\n   198\t    command = sys.argv[1] if len(sys.argv) > 1 else ''\n   199\t    if command == 'send' and len(sys.argv) == 4 and not sys.argv[2].startswith('-'):\n   200\t        send(Path(sys.argv[2]), float(sys.argv[3]))\n   201\t    elif command == 'rehearse' and len(sys.argv) == 4 and not sys.argv[2].startswith('-'):\n   202\t        import probe_rehearsal\n   203\t        probe_rehearsal.main(Path(sys.argv[2]), sys.argv[3])\n   204\t    else:\n   205\t        raise SystemExit(__doc__)\n     1\t\"\"\"Reading packets and the one verdict of the paid acceptance probe (PROBE-DESIGN.md v5 §3, §4; D716).\n     2\t\n     3\t  python3 probe_read.py packets <probe out folder>              # Part B and Part C packets for the hand reading (and a blind copy)\n     4\t  python3 probe_read.py verdict <probe out folder> <readings>   # the ordered verdict from the answers and the final readings\n     5\t\n     6\tReadings file (JSON): {\"B\": {\"<key>|<draw>|<target>\": {\"class\": ..., \"valid_support\": bool}}, \"C\": {\"<key>\": {\"read\": true,\n     7\t\"harms\": [{\"kind\": \"a|b|c|d\", \"status\": \"confirmed|unresolved\"}]}}}. A Part B target id is the bad id for an evidence target and\n     8\t\"placement\" for a placement target. Classes: intended, unsupported, misattributed, omitted (evidence); correct, absent, misattributed\n     9\t(placement); ambiguous (either, counts neither way).\n    10\t\"\"\"\n    11\timport json\n    12\timport re\n    13\timport sys\n    14\tfrom pathlib import Path\n    15\t\n    16\tHERE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\n    17\tPLAN, TARGETS, STORED_V7 = HERE / 'probe-plan.json', HERE / 'probe-targets.json', HERE / 'stored-v7-support.json'\n    18\tMISATTRIBUTION_TOLERANCE = 2\n    19\tCLASSES = {'intended', 'unsupported', 'misattributed', 'omitted', 'correct', 'absent', 'ambiguous'}\n    20\t\n    21\t\n    22\tdef load_answers(out):\n    23\t    lines = [json.loads(line) for line in (Path(out) / 'answers.jsonl').read_text().splitlines() if line.strip()] if (Path(out) / 'answers.jsonl').exists() else []\n    24\t    return {(l['part'], l['key'], l['form'], l['draw']): l for l in lines}\n    25\t\n    26\t\n    27\tdef target_ids(target):\n    28\t    return target['bad'] if target['kind'] == 'evidence' else 'placement'\n    29\t\n    30\t\n    31\tdef entries(user):\n    32\t    return {m.group(1): m.group(0) for m in re.finditer(r'^- (e\\d+) \\[[^\\n]*(?:\\n    [^\\n]*)*', user, re.M)}\n    33\t\n    34\t\n    35\tdef verdict(answers, readings, plan, targets, stored_v7, summary):\n    36\t    \"\"\"PROBE-DESIGN.md v5 §3: the first rule that applies.\"\"\"\n    37\t    keys = lambda items: [f'{i[\"source\"]}:{i[\"call_id\"]}' for i in items]\n    38\t    a1, a0 = keys(plan['acceptance'][:2])\n    39\t    reasons = []\n    40\t    for part, key in (('A1', a1), ('A0', a0)):\n    41\t        line = answers.get((part, key, 'v12', 1))\n    42\t        if line and (line['status'] == 'format invalid' or (line['status'] == 'transport error' and line.get('http_status') == 400)):\n    43\t            return 'not ready (format)', [f'{part} rejected: {line.get(\"error\", \"\")[:200]}']\n    44\t    v12 = [l for l in answers.values() if l['form'] == 'v12' and l['part'] != 'A2']\n    45\t    refused = [l for l in v12 if l['status'] == 'format invalid' or (l['status'] == 'answered' and l['check'])]\n    46\t    if refused:\n    47\t        reasons.append(f'{len(refused)} v12 answers refused')\n    48\t    b_reads = readings.get('B', {})\n    49\t    misattributed = {k.rsplit('|', 1)[0] for k, r in b_reads.items() if r['class'] == 'misattributed'}\n    50\t    if len(misattributed) > MISATTRIBUTION_TOLERANCE:\n    51\t        reasons.append(f'{len(misattributed)} Part B answers with a confirmed misattribution (tolerance {MISATTRIBUTION_TOLERANCE})')\n    52\t    losses, unresolved = [], []\n    53\t    for request in targets['requests']:\n    54\t        for target in request['targets']:\n    55\t            if target['kind'] != 'evidence' or not target.get('material'):\n    56\t                continue\n    57\t            draws = [b_reads.get(f'{request[\"key\"]}|{d}|{target[\"bad\"]}') for d in (1, 2, 3)]\n    58\t            received = all(answers.get(('B', request['key'], 'v12', d), {}).get('status') in ('answered', 'format invalid') for d in (1, 2, 3))\n    59\t            if not received or any(r is None for r in draws):\n    60\t                continue                                                   # a loss needs all three draws received and read\n    61\t            if not any(r['valid_support'] for r in draws):\n    62\t                (losses if stored_v7['targets'].get(request['key'], {}).get('supported') else unresolved).append(f'{request[\"key\"]} {target[\"bad\"]}')\n    63\t    if losses:\n    64\t        reasons.append('confirmed material loss in Part B: ' + ', '.join(losses))\n    65\t    c_reads = readings.get('C', {})\n    66\t    harms = [f'{k} ({h[\"kind\"]})' for k, r in c_reads.items() for h in r.get('harms', []) if h['status'] == 'confirmed']\n    67\t    if harms:\n    68\t        reasons.append('confirmed material harm in Part C: ' + ', '.join(harms))\n    69\t    if reasons:\n    70\t        return 'not ready', reasons\n    71\t    incomplete = []\n    72\t    if summary.get('ledger', {}).get('stopped'):\n    73\t        incomplete.append(f'the ledger stopped: {summary[\"ledger\"].get(\"stop_reason\")}')\n    74\t    for part, key in (('A1', a1), ('A0', a0)):\n    75\t        line = answers.get((part, key, 'v12', 1))\n    76\t        if not line or line['status'] != 'answered':\n    77\t            incomplete.append(f'{part} has no result')\n    78\t    for key in keys(plan['refused']):\n    79\t        for d in (1, 2, 3):\n    80\t            line = answers.get(('B', key, 'v12', d))\n    81\t            if not line or line['status'] not in ('answered', 'format invalid'):\n    82\t                incomplete.append(f'Part B {key} draw {d} missing')\n    83\t            for request in targets['requests']:\n    84\t                if request['key'] == key:\n    85\t                    for target in request['targets']:\n    86\t                        if f'{key}|{d}|{target_ids(target)}' not in b_reads:\n    87\t                            incomplete.append(f'Part B {key} draw {d} {target_ids(target)} not read')\n    88\t    for key in keys(plan['matched']):\n    89\t        complete = all(answers.get(('C', key, form, d), {}).get('status') in ('answered', 'format invalid') for form in ('v12', 'v7') for d in (1, 2, 3))\n    90\t        if not complete:\n    91\t            incomplete.append(f'Part C {key} incomplete')\n    92\t        elif not c_reads.get(key, {}).get('read'):\n    93\t            incomplete.append(f'Part C {key} not read')\n    94\t    if incomplete:\n    95\t        return 'inconclusive (incomplete)', incomplete\n    96\t    unresolved += [f'{k} ({h[\"kind\"]})' for k, r in c_reads.items() for h in r.get('harms', []) if h['status'] == 'unresolved']\n    97\t    if unresolved:\n    98\t        return 'inconclusive (unresolved)', unresolved\n    99\t    return 'pass', [f'{len(misattributed)} Part B answers with a confirmed misattribution']\n   100\t\n   101\t\n   102\tdef packets(out):\n   103\t    out = Path(out)\n   104\t    plan, targets, answers = json.loads(PLAN.read_text()), json.loads(TARGETS.read_text()), load_answers(out)\n   105\t    by_key = {f'{i[\"source\"]}:{i[\"call_id\"]}': i for i in plan['refused'] + plan['matched']}\n   106\t    show = lambda l: None if not l or not l.get('data') else {k: l['data'].get(k) for k in ('rung', 'reference', 'implied_outcome', 'reasons', 'cites', 'cites_views', 'pushes', 'theme_pushes', 'changed')}\n   107\t    b, blind = [], []\n   108\t    for request in targets['requests']:\n   109\t        item, listed = by_key[request['key']], entries(by_key[request['key']]['user'])\n   110\t        for d in (1, 2, 3):\n   111\t            line = answers.get(('B', request['key'], 'v12', d))\n   112\t            text = json.dumps(show(line) or {}, ensure_ascii=False)\n   113\t            for target in request['targets']:\n   114\t                flags = [m for m in target.get('markers', []) if m.lower() not in text.lower()]\n   115\t                quotes = {e: listed.get(e, '(not listed)')[:600] for e in target.get('sources', []) + target.get('partial', []) + target.get('near_misses', [])}\n   116\t                entry = {'id': f'{request[\"key\"]}|{d}|{target_ids(target)}', 'status': line['status'] if line else 'missing', 'answer': show(line),\n   117\t                         'target': target, 'quotes': quotes, 'markers not found': flags, 'question': item['user'].split('\\n', 1)[0]}\n   118\t                b.append(entry)\n   119\t                blind.append(entry)\n   120\t    c = []\n   121\t    for item in plan['matched']:\n   122\t        key, listed = f'{item[\"source\"]}:{item[\"call_id\"]}', entries(item['user'])\n   123\t        arms = {form: [show(answers.get(('C', key, form, d))) for d in (1, 2, 3)] for form in ('v12', 'v7')}\n   124\t        cited = lambda a: set((a or {}).get('cites') or []) | {p['evidence_id'] for p in (a or {}).get('pushes') or []}\n   125\t        counts = {form: {} for form in arms}\n   126\t        for form, answers_ in arms.items():\n   127\t            for a in answers_:\n   128\t                for e in cited(a):\n   129\t                    counts[form][e] = counts[form].get(e, 0) + 1\n   130\t        differing = sorted(e for e in set(counts['v12']) | set(counts['v7']) if (counts['v12'].get(e, 0) >= 2) != (counts['v7'].get(e, 0) >= 2))\n   131\t        everything = sorted(set(counts['v12']) | set(counts['v7']))\n   132\t        c.append({'key': key, 'question': item['user'].split('\\n', 1)[0], 'stored answer': json.loads(item['stored answer']) if item.get('stored answer') else None,\n   133\t                  'v12': arms['v12'], 'v7': arms['v7'], 'rungs': {f: [a and a['rung'] for a in arms[f]] for f in arms},\n   134\t                  'differing sources (>=2 of 3 in one arm only)': differing, 'quotes': {e: listed.get(e, '(not listed)')[:600] for e in everything}})\n   135\t    (out / 'packet-B.json').write_text(json.dumps(b, ensure_ascii=False, indent=1))\n   136\t    (out / 'packet-C.json').write_text(json.dumps(c, ensure_ascii=False, indent=1))\n   137\t    print(f'Part B: {len(b)} target readings; Part C: {len(c)} comparisons')\n   138\t\n   139\t\n   140\tdef main():\n   141\t    if len(sys.argv) >= 3 and sys.argv[1] == 'packets':\n   142\t        packets(sys.argv[2])\n   143\t    elif len(sys.argv) == 4 and sys.argv[1] == 'verdict':\n   144\t        out = Path(sys.argv[2])\n   145\t        summary = json.loads((out / 'run-summary.json').read_text()) if (out / 'run-summary.json').exists() else {}\n   146\t        result = verdict(load_answers(out), json.loads(Path(sys.argv[3]).read_text()), json.loads(PLAN.read_text()), json.loads(TARGETS.read_text()),\n   147\t                         json.loads(STORED_V7.read_text()), summary)\n   148\t        print(json.dumps({'verdict': result[0], 'reasons': result[1]}, indent=1))\n   149\t    else:\n   150\t        raise SystemExit(__doc__)\n   151\t\n   152\t\n   153\tif __name__ == '__main__':\n   154\t    main()\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba PROBE-DESIGN.md | sed -n '36,250p'; nl -ba ../../../clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py | sed -n '90,167p;212,295p'; sed -n '10756,10780p' ../../DECISIONS-log.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba PROBE-DESIGN.md | sed -n '36,250p'; nl -ba ../../../clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py | sed -n '90,167p;212,295p'; sed -n '10756,10780p' ../../DECISIONS-log.md\"","aggregated_output":"    36\t- one ordered verdict.\n    37\t\n    38\tv5 answers round 40d (`codex-r40d.md`), and round 40e: a material loss needs all three draws received and read.\n    39\t- each draw's valid support is recorded apart from its class, and a material loss means no draw with valid support;\n    40\t- Part C's wrong attributions are counted by claim;\n    41\t- a missing A1 or A0 result counts as incomplete.\n    42\t\n    43\t## 1. What it decides\n    44\t\n    45\t| Question | Part |\n    46\t|---|---|\n    47\t| Q1. Does the provider accept judging-v12's format on a real request, the largest of the five archives included, and on an empty list? | A |\n    48\t| Q2. On the requests the open format let the model get wrong, does it now state each fact and cite a listed source for it, without a wrong listed id in its place, and without dropping a material fact? | B |\n    49\t| Q3. On ordinary requests, does the closed format change what the judge cites or concludes, beyond its own variation under the open format? | C |\n    50\t\n    51\t## 2. The sends, in this order\n    52\t\n    53\t1. **A1:** old-1 call 5652, the largest stored request of the five archives (451 evidence ids). Its `cites_views` is empty, so it\n    54\t   also exercises `maxItems: 0`.\n    55\t2. **A0:** old-3 call 69, a request with an empty theme list (`theme_pushes` with `maxItems: 0`); under $0.001.\n    56\t3. **Part B:** the 16 distinct refused requests, 3 sends each under v12's format.\n    57\t   - control-1's 8941 is 8938's retry: one request, both attempts' bad ids targeted.\n    58\t   - linked-1's 7 requests keep their stored judging-v8 text; only the answer format changes. That makes them a format probe on\n    59\t     those texts. No v8-based version is built.\n    60\t4. **Part C:** 12 matched comparisons, one per (source, question) of the refused set. Each is the same question's accepted\n    61\t   first-attempt request in the same archive with the closest evidence count; ties go to the nearest call on either side, which is\n    62\t   what `probe_plan.py` does.\n    63\t   - Each comparison is 3 sends under v12's format and 3 under judging-v7's open format (the fresh control).\n    64\t   - Comparisons run cheapest first. Within one comparison the six sends run one after another.\n    65\t   - The 16 refused requests map to 12 (source, question) pairs. The four duplicates are dropped to fit the ceiling, so every\n    66\t     question is covered once per source.\n    67\t5. **A2,** last and only if the headroom then covers its reservation ($0.0824): the sealed D358 run's call 6918 (647 ids) with v12's\n    68\t   format built from its lists. It is a size check on an older request text. A 200 shows that a request this size fits; a 400\n    69\t   establishes an enum limit only if the provider's error says so. Its answer is not read.\n    70\t\n    71\t**Start rule** (proved at $0 with `budget_replay.llm_estimate`):\n    72\t- Only one Part C comparison runs at a time.\n    73\t- It starts only when the ceiling minus spent minus reserved covers the sum of its six first attempts' reservations.\n    74\t- On the stored-token estimate all 12 start: lowest margin $0.037; expected core spend $0.347.\n    75\t- If every send costs 30% more than stored, only 10 start in this order: the 11th needs $0.136 with $0.107 left.\n    76\t- A retry reserves again, so an admitted comparison can still stop incomplete.\n    77\t- A comparison not started, or stopped, makes Part C incomplete, and the outcome inconclusive.\n    78\t\n    79\tEach part's sends run at most 4 at a time. Every send gets its own archive (per part, request, format and draw), so `model.call`\n    80\tnever answers a draw from an earlier draw: every draw is a fresh provider call, counted at the transport.\n    81\t\n    82\tA transport error is recorded. The budget transport retries a 429 or 5xx as it does in production, and settles an error at its\n    83\treservation.\n    84\t\n    85\t## 3. Reading rule (frozen)\n    86\t\n    87\t### Checks on every answer\n    88\tEvery answer is checked as at request time, with a harness check proved equal to `check_answer` on fixtures and on the stored\n    89\tanswers (§4):\n    90\t- membership against the request's lists;\n    91\t- the rung range from the request's ladder line;\n    92\t- first-judgement and changed against the request's \"[Previous conclusion …]\" line;\n    93\t- non-empty stance fields;\n    94\t- duplicate theme pushes.\n    95\t\n    96\tThe archive's final ledger state is not used: it falsely refuses stored answers such as 8834 and 8851 (Codex r40).\n    97\t\n    98\t### Part B (48 answers)\n    99\tEach answer is read against `probe-targets.json`.\n   100\t- **Evidence targets.** One class each, judged by the claim each cited or pushed entry is used for:\n   101\t  - *intended*: the claim is stated, an entry in `sources` is used for it, and no other entry is used for it without carrying it;\n   102\t  - *unsupported*: stated, with no entry in `sources`. An entry in `partial` alone leaves the exact claim unsupported, but is not a\n   103\t    wrong attribution;\n   104\t  - *misattributed*: an entry is used for the claim while its quote does not carry it. This counts even if the entry supports a\n   105\t    different claim in the same answer, or a correct source is also cited;\n   106\t  - *omitted*: the claim is not stated.\n   107\t  - The class is judged on the target's `required` claim against `sources`. An `optional` detail stated without its own source is\n   108\t    unsupported for that detail only, recorded, and does not change the class.\n   109\t  - When more than one class applies, misattributed comes first, then intended, then unsupported, then omitted. A wrong source with\n   110\t    no correct one is misattributed.\n   111\t  - Apart from the class, each draw records **valid support**: the required claim is stated and an entry in `sources` is used for\n   112\t    it, whether or not a wrong source is also used. The material-loss rules count draws without valid support, whatever their class.\n   113\t  A `markers` search in the answer's text flags the reader's attention; the hand reading decides.\n   114\t- **Placement targets.**\n   115\t  - *correct*: the id appears only in its own field;\n   116\t  - *absent*: not named;\n   117\t  - a substitute evidence id carrying no claim the answer states is *misattributed*.\n   118\t- **Ambiguous targets** (two acceptable sources, or an unclear fact) are reported and count neither way.\n   119\t- **A second, blind reader** (Codex) reads the 48 against the frozen targets. A disagreement goes to a third, source-backed read whose\n   120\t  class decides.\n   121\t\n   122\t### Part C (12 comparisons, all 72 answers read)\n   123\t- Every answer is read in full: its reference, implied outcome, reasons, and the claim each cited or pushed source is used for,\n   124\t  shared sources included.\n   125\t- The numbers only order the reading:\n   126\t  - the sources cited by at least 2 of 3 answers in one arm and at most 1 of 3 in the other;\n   127\t  - any v12 rung outside the range of the v7 rungs.\n   128\t- A v7 answer the request-time check refuses is still read as an answer, and its refusal is recorded (it is the failure the closed\n   129\t  format removes). A comparison is complete with its 3 + 3 answers.\n   130\t\n   131\tA **material harm** is any of these, repeated (in at least 2 of 3 v12 answers and at most 1 of 3 v7 answers), counted by claim, not by\n   132\tsource id:\n   133\t- (a) a claim that moves the forecast or the reference, which at least 2 of 3 v7 answers state with a listed source carrying it (any\n   134\t  such source: one control citing e195 and another e669 for the $393 billion reference count as two), and which at least 2 of 3 v12\n   135\t  answers do not state with a carrying source;\n   136\t- (b) a claim that at least 2 of 3 v12 answers attribute to a source whose quote does not carry it, counted by claim whichever\n   137\t  sources are used. For example, \"the market reference is $390 billion\" attributed to e195 in one answer and e669 in another, while\n   138\t  both entries give $393 billion;\n   139\t- (c) a changed reference or implied outcome whose stated support is a citation of kind (a) or (b);\n   140\t- (d) a v12 rung outside the v7 range whose reasons trace to (a), (b) or (c).\n   141\t\n   142\tA difference that is not repeated, or whose cause cannot be read, is **unresolved**.\n   143\t\n   144\t### Outcome (registered; proposed tolerances for this probe, not historical rates)\n   145\tOne verdict, taken from the first rule that applies:\n   146\t1. **Not ready (format):** A1 or A0 is rejected or returns a format-invalid answer.\n   147\t2. **Not ready (confirmed failure):** any of\n   148\t   - a v12 answer refused by the request-time check;\n   149\t   - more than 2 of 48 Part B answers with a confirmed misattribution;\n   150\t   - a confirmed material loss in Part B;\n   151\t   - a confirmed material harm in Part C.\n   152\t\n   153\t   A confirmed failure stands even when the run is incomplete.\n   154\t3. **Inconclusive (incomplete):** a budget stop; A1 or A0 without a result (a transport failure or timeout, as opposed to a format\n   155\t   rejection); a missing Part B answer; or a Part C comparison not started or interrupted.\n   156\t4. **Inconclusive (unresolved):** an unresolved material loss in Part B, or an unresolved Part C difference that would be material if\n   157\t   confirmed.\n   158\t5. **Pass (\"ready to propose adoption\"):** otherwise.\n   159\t\n   160\tA2, sent, skipped or rejected, never changes the verdict; it is reported. The conditions behind these rules:\n   161\t- **Pass,** when every condition holds:\n   162\t  - Q1: A1 and A0 return 200 with format-valid answers;\n   163\t  - all 48 Part B answers and all 12 Part C comparisons (72 answers) are complete;\n   164\t  - no v12 answer is refused by the request-time check;\n   165\t  - in Part B, at most 2 of 48 answers have a confirmed misattribution (an answer counts once), with the number of requests affected\n   166\t    and any repetition reported;\n   167\t  - no confirmed material loss in Part B: a material target whose three draws were all received and read, none with valid support\n   168\t    (whatever each draw's class), which the stored accepted v7 answer to the same request stated and supported;\n   169\t  - no confirmed material harm in Part C.\n   170\t- **Inconclusive:**\n   171\t  - a budget stop, a missing answer, a comparison not started or interrupted;\n   172\t  - an unresolved material loss in Part B: a material target whose three draws were all received and read, none with valid support,\n   173\t    where no stored accepted v7 answer to that request kept it, as in control-1's 8938, whose retry also dropped 85.4%;\n   174\t  - an unresolved Part C difference that would be material if confirmed.\n   175\t\n   176\tThe outcome is computed by code (`probe_read.py`) from the read classes; the rehearsal exercises it (§4).\n   177\t- **Not ready:** any other failure of the pass conditions, with its reason.\n   178\t- Every outcome goes to Alex; adoption is his decision.\n   179\t\n   180\t## 4. Harness and the $0 rehearsal before the send\n   181\t\n   182\t`probe.py`, harness-only:\n   183\t- it reads `probe-plan.json` and builds each request with `model.build_request`, from poc-v121's setting and v12's format (or v7's\n   184\t  for the control);\n   185\t- it sends through `budget_replay.BudgetTransport` on a ledger at $0.50, in the order and under the start rule of §2;\n   186\t- each answer goes through `model.call`'s format check and the request-time check;\n   187\t- each answer is written to `probe-answers.jsonl` with its part, request, format, draw, the request sha, the cost and the transport's\n   188\t  call number.\n   189\t- `probe_read.py` builds the reading packets:\n   190\t  - Part B by target, with marker flags;\n   191\t  - Part C by comparison: all six answers in full, the quote of every source any of them cites (shared ones included), and the\n   192\t    symmetric-difference sources marked.\n   193\t- `probe_read.py` also computes the one verdict of §3 from the read classes.\n   194\t\n   195\t**The $0 rehearsal** uses the real budget transport with the provider stubbed underneath (`model.openai_transport` replaced), on a\n   196\tledger file of its own. It must show:\n   197\t- every scheduled send reaches the stub, with a count equal to the plan: 2 + 1 for A, 48 for B, 72 for C;\n   198\t- each request's bytes: system and user equal the stored ones, the format strict and equal to `schema_for('judging-v12', lists)` (or\n   199\t  v7's), the model settings as poc-v121's;\n   200\t- three fresh stub calls per draw set;\n   201\t- the request-time check equals `check_answer` on a ledger fixture whose state is known, accepts every stored committed answer of the\n   202\t  planned requests, and refuses the stored refused ones on their ids;\n   203\t- the stub's valid answer, a format-invalid answer, an HTTP 400 and a 5xx followed by success each take their path;\n   204\t- only one Part C comparison runs at a time;\n   205\t- a ceiling set low blocks a Part C start, and the outcome is \"inconclusive\", never \"pass\";\n   206\t- a retry exhausts the remaining headroom inside an admitted comparison, which stops it; the outcome is \"inconclusive\";\n   207\t- the outcome code's verdicts:\n   208\t  - three Part B answers for control-1's 8938 that state 85.4% with no source are an unresolved material loss, so \"inconclusive\"\n   209\t    (8938 has no stored accepted v7 answer);\n   210\t  - three answers for control-1's 8807 that state the $393 billion reference with no source are a confirmed material loss, so \"not\n   211\t    ready\" (its stored accepted retry 8809 cites e195 and e669);\n   212\t  - three misattributions are \"not ready\";\n   213\t  - for 8807, two draws giving the $393 billion reference with a wrong source and a third omitting it: within the misattribution\n   214\t    tolerance, but a confirmed material loss, so \"not ready\";\n   215\t  - A1 timing out after the transport's retries is \"inconclusive (incomplete)\", told apart from an explicit format rejection;\n   216\t  - for 8807, one unsupported draw and two draws missing after a budget stop: no material loss can be declared, so \"inconclusive\";\n   217\t  - a clean set is \"pass\";\n   218\t  - an A1 rejection is \"not ready (format)\", even though it also leaves an answer missing;\n   219\t  - a confirmed misattribution excess with Part C incomplete is \"not ready\";\n   220\t  - an unresolved material Part C difference with everything else clean is \"inconclusive\";\n   221\t  - A2 skipped, and A2 rejected, each leave a clean core \"pass\";\n   222\t- the Part B packet for 8938 flags a stub answer that drops \"85.4\".\n   223\t\n   224\tA mutant, Part B sent with the open format, is caught by the byte check.\n    90\t\n    91\tclass SharedLedger:\n    92\t    \"\"\"One JSON ledger for every run under a ceiling, guarded by an exclusive file lock (processes and threads). The first refused\n    93\t    reservation, or an explicit `stop`, persists `stopped` with its reason under the lock: every later reservation, in any thread or\n    94\t    process, is refused (WIRING-DESIGN.md §B2, D448).\"\"\"\n    95\t\n    96\t    def __init__(self, path):\n    97\t        self.path = Path(path)\n    98\t        self.lock_path = self.path.with_suffix('.lock')\n    99\t        self.attempts_path = self.path.with_suffix('.attempts.jsonl')   # one line per settled or refused attempt: the measurement record\n   100\t\n   101\t    def _note(self, entry):\n   102\t        \"\"\"Append one attempt line (the process, the call kind, the amounts, the tokens when reported, the moment) for per-component\n   103\t        spend and timing. Written only after the ledger's state is saved, and best-effort: a failed append never blocks a stop, a charge\n   104\t        or an overrun. A crash between the two writes leaves the lines short of the ledger, never ahead of it; the tally reports the gap\n   105\t        as unaccounted. One short append, so concurrent lines do not interleave.\"\"\"\n   106\t        line = json.dumps(dict(entry, pid=os.getpid(), at=time.strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S%z'))) + '\\n'\n   107\t        try:\n   108\t            with open(self.attempts_path, 'a') as handle:\n   109\t                handle.write(line)\n   110\t        except OSError:\n   111\t            pass\n   112\t\n   113\t    @contextlib.contextmanager\n   114\t    def _locked(self):\n   115\t        with open(self.lock_path, 'a+') as lock:\n   116\t            fcntl.flock(lock, fcntl.LOCK_EX)\n   117\t            try:\n   118\t                state = json.loads(self.path.read_text())\n   119\t                yield state\n   120\t                temporary = self.path.with_suffix('.tmp')\n   121\t                temporary.write_text(json.dumps(state, indent=1))\n   122\t                os.replace(temporary, self.path)          # a reader never sees a half-written ledger\n   123\t            finally:\n   124\t                fcntl.flock(lock, fcntl.LOCK_UN)\n   125\t\n   126\t    @staticmethod\n   127\t    def init(path, ceiling):\n   128\t        Path(path).write_text(json.dumps({'ceiling': ceiling, 'spent': 0.0, 'reserved': 0.0, 'overrun': False, 'refused': 0, 'attempts': 0,\n   129\t                                          'stopped': False, 'stop_reason': None}, indent=1))\n   130\t\n   131\t    def reserve(self, amount):\n   132\t        with self._locked() as state:\n   133\t            granted = not (state.get('stopped') or state['overrun'] or state['spent'] + state['reserved'] + amount > state['ceiling'])\n   134\t            if granted:\n   135\t                state['reserved'] += amount\n   136\t                state['attempts'] += 1\n   137\t            else:\n   138\t                state['refused'] += 1\n   139\t                if not state.get('stopped'):\n   140\t                    state['stopped'] = True\n   141\t                    state['stop_reason'] = 'overrun' if state['overrun'] else f'a reservation of ${amount:.6f} would pass the ${state[\"ceiling\"]:.2f} ceiling'\n   142\t        if not granted:\n   143\t            self._note({'refused': amount})                  # after the stop is saved\n   144\t            return False\n   145\t        _LIVE.depth = getattr(_LIVE, 'depth', 0) + 1\n   146\t        return True\n   147\t\n   148\t    @staticmethod\n   149\t    def estimate(request):\n   150\t        \"\"\"The shared reservation of one language-model attempt (WIRING-DESIGN.md §B): `llm_estimate`.\"\"\"\n   151\t        return llm_estimate(request)\n   152\t\n   153\t    def settle(self, reserved, actual, kind='llm', tokens=None):\n   154\t        \"\"\"Settle one attempt. A missing, non-finite, zero or negative charge settles at the whole reservation: an answered paid\n   155\t        request never costs nothing, and a failed attempt is charged its reservation. `kind` (llm, jev, embeddings) and the reported\n   156\t        `tokens` go to the attempt line only.\"\"\"\n   157\t        _LIVE.depth = max(0, getattr(_LIVE, 'depth', 0) - 1)\n   158\t        if not isinstance(actual, (int, float)) or isinstance(actual, bool) or not math.isfinite(actual) or actual <= 0:\n   159\t            actual = reserved\n   160\t        with self._locked() as state:\n   161\t            state['reserved'] = max(0.0, state['reserved'] - reserved)\n   162\t            state['spent'] += actual\n   163\t            if actual > reserved + 1e-12:\n   164\t                state['overrun'] = True\n   165\t                if not state.get('stopped'):\n   166\t                    state['stopped'], state['stop_reason'] = True, 'overrun'\n   167\t        self._note({'kind': kind, 'reserved': reserved, 'charged': actual, **({'tokens': tokens} if tokens is not None else {})})\n   212\t    def stop(self, reason):\n   213\t        \"\"\"A stop any component records: every later reservation is refused.\"\"\"\n   214\t        with self._locked() as state:\n   215\t            if not state.get('stopped'):\n   216\t                state['stopped'], state['stop_reason'] = True, reason\n   217\t\n   218\t    def read(self):\n   219\t        with open(self.lock_path, 'a+') as lock:\n   220\t            fcntl.flock(lock, fcntl.LOCK_EX)\n   221\t            try:\n   222\t                return json.loads(self.path.read_text())\n   223\t            finally:\n   224\t                fcntl.flock(lock, fcntl.LOCK_UN)\n   225\t\n   226\t\n   227\tdef llm_estimate(request):\n   228\t    price_in, price_out = model.PRICES[request['model']]\n   229\t    cap = request.get('max_completion_tokens', request.get('max_tokens'))\n   230\t    if isinstance(cap, bool) or not isinstance(cap, int) or cap <= 0:\n   231\t        raise model.TransportError('request without a positive output cap: refused by the budget')\n   232\t    tokens_in = 2 * len(json.dumps(request).encode('utf-8')) + 4096\n   233\t    return (tokens_in * price_in + cap * price_out) / 1e6\n   234\t\n   235\t\n   236\tdef whole(count):\n   237\t    return isinstance(count, int) and not isinstance(count, bool) and count >= 0\n   238\t\n   239\t\n   240\tdef llm_cost(response, request):\n   241\t    \"\"\"The answer's cost by `model.call`'s formula; None (settled at the reservation) unless the counts are whole, nonnegative numbers\n   242\t    with some input.\"\"\"\n   243\t    usage = response.get('usage') if isinstance(response, dict) else None\n   244\t    if not isinstance(usage, dict):\n   245\t        return None\n   246\t    tokens_in, tokens_out = usage.get('prompt_tokens'), usage.get('completion_tokens')\n   247\t    details = usage.get('prompt_tokens_details') or {}\n   248\t    cached = (details.get('cached_tokens') or 0) if isinstance(details, dict) else None\n   249\t    if not (whole(tokens_in) and whole(tokens_out) and whole(cached)) or tokens_in == 0:\n   250\t        return None\n   251\t    price_in, price_out = model.PRICES[request['model']]\n   252\t    cached = min(tokens_in, cached)\n   253\t    return (tokens_in - cached) / 1e6 * price_in + cached / 1e6 * price_in * model.CACHED_INPUT_SHARE + tokens_out / 1e6 * price_out\n   254\t\n   255\t\n   256\tdef jev_estimate(request):\n   257\t    price_in, _ = model.PRICES[request['model']]\n   258\t    tokens_in = 2 * len(json.dumps(request, sort_keys=True, ensure_ascii=False).encode('utf-8')) + 4096\n   259\t    return jev.ATTEMPTS * tokens_in * price_in / 1e6\n   260\t\n   261\t\n   262\tclass BudgetTransport:\n   263\t    \"\"\"Called as production calls a transport: (provider, request) for a language model, (request,) for Jev.\"\"\"\n   264\t\n   265\t    def __init__(self, ledger, sleep=time.sleep):\n   266\t        self.ledger, self.sleep = ledger, sleep\n   267\t\n   268\t    def __call__(self, *args):\n   269\t        if len(args) == 1:\n   270\t            return self._jev(args[0])\n   271\t        provider, request = args\n   272\t        for attempt in range(3):\n   273\t            estimate = llm_estimate(request)\n   274\t            if not self.ledger.reserve(estimate):\n   275\t                raise model.TransportError('the shared budget ceiling would be passed: not sent')\n   276\t            try:\n   277\t                response = model.openai_transport(provider, request, max_attempts=1)\n   278\t            except model.TransportError as error:\n   279\t                self.ledger.settle(estimate, estimate)\n   280\t                status = getattr(error, 'http_status', None)\n   281\t                if status in CLIENT_ERRORS or attempt == 2 or (status is not None and status != 429 and status < 500):\n   282\t                    raise\n   283\t                self.sleep(5 * (attempt + 1))\n   284\t                continue\n   285\t            except Exception:\n   286\t                self.ledger.settle(estimate, estimate)\n   287\t                raise\n   288\t            cost = llm_cost(response, request)\n   289\t            self.ledger.settle(estimate, estimate if cost is None else cost)\n   290\t            return response\n   291\t        raise model.TransportError('no answer after three attempts')\n   292\t\n   293\t    def _jev(self, request):\n   294\t        estimate = jev_estimate(request)\n   295\t        if not self.ledger.reserve(estimate):\n## D715 · 2026-11-22 · Alex approves $0.50 for the paid acceptance step of judging-v12\n\n- **The question:** \"引用格式的新版本已经做好，所有不花钱的验证都通过了。要不要花一点钱实测？实测这样做：先发最大的一次请求和一次名单为空的请求，确认服务商接受这个格式；再把当初被退回的 17 个请求和 17 个正常请求用新版本重发，人工对照原文看模型有没有选对证据。每个请求发一次，约 0.10 美元；各发三次看稳不稳，约 0.30 美元。发之前我会先和审查员定好怎么读、怎么判。\"\n  Options: 0.5 美元 (recommended: three sends per request with a margin; a stop above $0.50; the reading rule agreed with the council\n  before the send; Claude reads the results); 0.15 美元 (one send per request); 先不花 (stop; poc-v118 stays the product).\n- **Alex's answer** (2026-11-22): \"0.5 美元 (推荐)\".\n- **Next:** the probe design and its reading rule through the council at $0, the harness dry-run at $0, then the send under a $0.50\n  reservation ledger.\n\n## D716 · 2026-11-22 · Council R passes the paid acceptance probe's design (round 40, six passes); the harness and its $0 rehearsal next\n\n- **Design:** `docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/PROBE-DESIGN.md` v5, with `probe-plan.json` and `probe-targets.json`. The targets\n  were frozen before any send and amended twice before any send.\n  - **Sends:** A1 (the largest request), A0 (an empty theme list); Part B, 16 refused requests × 3 under v12; Part C, 12 matched\n    comparisons, 3 under v12 and 3 under v7, one comparison at a time, each starting only if its worst-case reservations fit; A2, the\n    sealed 647-id request, last and conditional.\n  - **Reading:** by claim, with required and optional details. Each draw's valid support is recorded apart from its class. All 72 Part C\n    answers are read in full.\n  - **Verdict:** format failure → confirmed failure (standing even when incomplete) → incomplete → unresolved → pass. Pass requires at\n    most 2 of 48 confirmed misattributions, no confirmed material loss (three draws received and read, none with valid support, where\n    the stored accepted v7 answer had it), and no confirmed material harm in Part C.\n  - **Expected spend:** $0.35. At 130% of stored costs, 10 of 12 comparisons start, giving inconclusive.\n- **Council** (`codex-r40.md` … `codex-r40f.md`): 40 to 40e NOT READY, each finding taken; 40f READY TO BUILD THE HARNESS.\n- **Found while freezing the targets:** most refused ids are real evidence ids. Two (e88, e2769) are unlisted ids that the frozen\n  request itself names in \"same claim as …\" notes, which is a latent invitation. e393 is the $393 billion reference written as an id.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
