{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'import json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom unittest.mock import patch\nimport probe, probe_read, probe_rehearsal as r\np=r.PLAN; raw=json.loads(probe_read.TARGETS.read_text()); hist=json.loads(probe_read.STORED_V7.read_text())\na=r.clean_answers()\nreads=r.clean_readings({f'\\\\''B/control-1:8807|{d}|e393'\\\\'':{'\\\\''class'\\\\'':'\\\\''unsupported'\\\\'','\\\\''valid_support'\\\\'':'\\\\''false'\\\\''} for d in (1,2,3)})\nprint('\\\\''three unsupported signed as strings:'\\\\'',probe_read.verdict(a,reads,p,raw,hist,{})[0])\nclass Needle:\n    def __init__(self): self.out=Path('\\\\''/virtual'\\\\''); self.ledger=self; self.seen=[]\n    def send(self,s):\n        self.seen.append(s['\\\\''part'\\\\''])\n        return {'\\\\''status'\\\\'':'\\\\''transport error'\\\\'','\\\\''http_status'\\\\'':400} if s['\\\\''part'\\\\'']=='\\\\''A1'\\\\'' else {'\\\\''status'\\\\'':'\\\\''answered'\\\\''}\n    def reservation(self,s):return 0.01\n    def headroom(self):return 0.50,{}\n    def read(self):return {}\nn=Needle()\nwith patch.object(Path,'\\\\''write_text'\\\\'',lambda *args,**kwargs:None):\n    probe.Probe.run(n,p)\nfrom collections import Counter\nprint('\\\\''post-A1 real scheduler steps after 400:'\\\\'',Counter(n.seen[1:]))\n'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'import json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom unittest.mock import patch\nimport probe, probe_read, probe_rehearsal as r\np=r.PLAN; raw=json.loads(probe_read.TARGETS.read_text()); hist=json.loads(probe_read.STORED_V7.read_text())\na=r.clean_answers()\nreads=r.clean_readings({f'\\\\''B/control-1:8807|{d}|e393'\\\\'':{'\\\\''class'\\\\'':'\\\\''unsupported'\\\\'','\\\\''valid_support'\\\\'':'\\\\''false'\\\\''} for d in (1,2,3)})\nprint('\\\\''three unsupported signed as strings:'\\\\'',probe_read.verdict(a,reads,p,raw,hist,{})[0])\nclass Needle:\n    def __init__(self): self.out=Path('\\\\''/virtual'\\\\''); self.ledger=self; self.seen=[]\n    def send(self,s):\n        self.seen.append(s['\\\\''part'\\\\''])\n        return {'\\\\''status'\\\\'':'\\\\''transport error'\\\\'','\\\\''http_status'\\\\'':400} if s['\\\\''part'\\\\'']=='\\\\''A1'\\\\'' else {'\\\\''status'\\\\'':'\\\\''answered'\\\\''}\n    def reservation(self,s):return 0.01\n    def headroom(self):return 0.50,{}\n    def read(self):return {}\nn=Needle()\nwith patch.object(Path,'\\\\''write_text'\\\\'',lambda *args,**kwargs:None):\n    probe.Probe.run(n,p)\nfrom collections import Counter\nprint('\\\\''post-A1 real scheduler steps after 400:'\\\\'',Counter(n.seen[1:]))\n'\"","aggregated_output":"three unsupported signed as strings: pass\npost-A1 real scheduler steps after 400: Counter({'C': 72, 'B': 48, 'A0': 1, 'A2': 1})\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"agent_message","text":"**NOT READY.** I reproduced verdict and spending failures offline. No paid calls were made.\n\n1. **The sender keeps spending after a required format check fails.** With A1 returning HTTP 400, the scheduler still attempts A0, all 48 Part B draws, all 72 Part C draws, and A2 if budget permits. D715 puts the format checks before the comparisons so they can establish whether to proceed. Rehearse that a required format rejection triggers zero B and C calls. [Sender](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/probe.py:144) · [D715](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:10756)\n\n2. **A2 can change a clean verdict.** At the planned core spend of $0.347, A2’s first $0.0824 reservation fits. If that attempt returns 503, the retry reservation stops the ledger. The verdict then changes from **pass** to **inconclusive**, contrary to the design. Preserve the core verdict when the optional check exhausts its headroom, and test this through the real budget transport. [A2 scheduling](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/probe.py:166) · [Verdict](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/probe_read.py:71)\n\n3. **The verdict accepts unreadable answers and malformed readings.** A Part C control logged as `format invalid` with no answer data still counts toward the six required answers. For `8807`, three unsupported readings with JSON `\"false\"` in place of boolean `false` also return **pass**. Require readable answers and validate the reading values before counting them. A readable v7 answer refused by the request-time check still counts as designed. [Verdict checks](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/probe_read.py:48)\n\n4. **The packets and records omit information needed to verify the result.** The Part C packet for `linked-1:8834` omits the source text for its cited dependency and two theme pushes. Part B supplies quotes only for preselected IDs, so a new wrong citation can appear without its quote. The send record also lacks the required transport call number and does not report charges on failed attempts. [Packets](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/probe_read.py:102) · [Send records](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/probe.py:120)\n\n5. **The rehearsal checks schema equality without checking wire bytes.** I reversed the schema’s property order. The serialized request changed, but the stub reported no problem. Compare the complete serialized request against an independently built expected request, and add a mutation that changes only property order. [Rehearsal stub](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/probe_rehearsal.py:45)"}}
